      "widgets_values": [
        "Two references, with different jobs.\n\nVideo 1 is the LAYOUT reference. Take from it: the camera move, the framing, the position and walk of the man, and where every object sits in the frame. Take its geometry as the plan of the shot.\n\nPicture 1 is the MATERIAL AND LIGHT reference. Take from it: what real brick, real ironwork, real foliage, real stone paving and real sunlight look like in this garden. Take nothing else from Picture 1 -- not its framing, not its viewpoint, not its composition.\n\nVideo 1 is a rough gaussian-splat previsualisation, not finished footage. Deliver the same shot as real live-action photography: a 35mm film frame of a real garden, shot on a fast prime, shallow depth of field, fine grain, soft highlight halation, restrained natural colour.\n\nThe scene: A sunlit garden beside an old red brick house with stone steps and tall windows, a metal pergola frame, lush green borders, potted plants and a wooden bench, a paved path across a bright lawn. Lit exactly like <Picture 1>: hard directional sunlight from the front-left, crisp shadows falling across the lawn and path, warm sunlit brick, deep green foliage, clear blue sky. Photographic, cinematic, 35mm film.\n\nDo not carry any of these defects from Video 1 into the output: no smeared or melted surfaces, no blurred undefined geometry, no low-resolution mush, no floating semi-transparent blobs, no dissolving or feathered edges on solid objects, no flat washed-out regions without texture, no compositing seam or halo around the man, no painted or illustrated look, no video-game render look.\n\nKeep the man exactly as he is in Video 1: same face, same short blond hair, same plain white crew-neck t-shirt, same loose mid-blue denim jeans, same white sneakers, same wristwatch on his left wrist, same walk and same timing.\n\nTimeline:\n[0s-4s] the man walks forward along the path toward camera, sunlight from the front-left across his face and shoulders, his shadow falling behind and to his right on the paving.\n[4s-8s] he keeps walking toward camera and looks up, the brick house and pergola passing behind him, the sunlit lawn filling the foreground.\n\nCamera: follow the reference video's camera exactly, one continuous move, no cuts.\n\nAudio: quiet garden ambience, birdsong, a faint breeze in the leaves."
      ]
    },
