        "Node name for S&R": "MiniMaxH3ReferenceToVideo"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "Two references, with different jobs.\n\nVideo 1 is the LAYOUT reference: a rough gaussian-splat previsualisation of this exact shot. Follow it precisely, frame for frame -- the camera move, the framing, the timing, and where every object sits in every frame. Match its geometry exactly; stay locked to it, do not advance ahead of it and do not invent new camera motion.\n\nPicture 1 is the MATERIAL AND LIGHT reference. Take from it what real brick, ironwork, foliage, stone paving and sunlight look like in this garden. Take nothing else from Picture 1 -- not its framing or viewpoint.\n\nVideo 1 is previsualisation, not finished footage. Deliver the same shot as real live-action photography: a 35mm film frame of a real garden, shot on a fast prime, shallow depth of field, fine grain, soft highlight halation, restrained natural colour.\n\nThe scene: A sunlit garden beside an old red brick house with stone steps and tall windows, a metal pergola frame, lush green borders, potted plants and a wooden bench, a paved path across a bright lawn. Lit exactly like <Picture 1>: hard directional sunlight from the front-left, crisp shadows falling across the lawn and path, warm sunlit brick, deep green foliage, clear blue sky. Photographic, cinematic, 35mm film.\n\nRebuild the previsualisation's rough surfaces as real, sharply detailed ones, but keep every surface in exactly the same place and shape: no smeared or melted surfaces, no blurred undefined geometry, no low-resolution mush, no floating semi-transparent blobs, no dissolving or feathered edges on solid objects, no flat washed-out regions without texture, no painted or illustrated look, no video-game render look.\n\nCamera: follow Video 1's camera exactly, one continuous move, no cuts.\n\nAudio: quiet garden ambience, birdsong, a faint breeze in the leaves.",
        1344,
        768,
        73,
        "max"
      ]
    },
